    "name": "oiv_prod_usd (base) - MultiSend unwrappers on the sub + manager Roles Modifiers",
    "description": "setTransactionUnwrapper on the sub Roles Modifier 0xB15400Bb735CF9d91E09d097f2dA588ebe760D49 and the manager Roles Modifier 0x988A15711CCDF16C06010bb41AaEBF39e407cD7F, for both Safe MultiSend contracts. Both are owned by this Manager Safe 0x7Bb5e307eDf80630f153BD28789b4365eFe4cce3. A Roles Modifier permission-checks one call at a time, so without an unwrap adapter a batched multiSend(bytes) is an opaque delegatecall it cannot decompose and rejects wholesale. The kUSD stack was deployed by the pre-fix KpkOivFactory on FIVE chains (ethereum, optimism, gnosis, base, arbitrum) at IDENTICAL modifier addresses, and all three modifiers on every one of them are missing both registrations - verified on-chain 2026-07-24. Execute the matching file on each chain; this one is base (chainId 8453). The exec Roles Modifier is owned by the OIV Safe - see oiv-prod-usd-unwrappers-base-oiv-safe.json.",
